# The operator dashboard was published here by mistake and is now built to
# reports/ instead (commit 7e48923). The asset is gone from this tree and the
# validate:published-tree-purity check HARD_FAILs if it ever comes back, but a
# deleted asset only 404s -- it does not stop the route from being re-created.
#
# Cloudflare Pages evaluates _redirects before asset lookup: "Redirects are
# always followed, regardless of whether or not an asset matches the incoming
# request." So this line makes /agency permanently non-serving at the origin
# even if a future build drops a file back at that path.
#
# Pages _redirects supports only 301/302/303/307/308 -- 404 and 410 are not
# valid status codes in this file -- so this is a 301 to the site root rather
# than the 410 the route deserves. A Pages Function would be required for 410.
/agency/* / 301
/agency / 301
